+# Heads Up
+
+A Codex Stop-hook plugin inspired by [You Should Know](https://x.com/ClaudeDevs/status/2106118517447876618).
+After a final response, an independent reviewer looks for one consequential
+implication the response did not clearly explain. A finding appears through
+Codex's existing hook warning display:
+
+> Heads Up · Payment retries could double-charge a customer unless the payment call is idempotent.
+
+Clean reviews stay quiet. Findings are advisory, require a quote from the source
+response, and never block completion or add instructions to the main conversation.
+This prototype does not include the demo's Learn more, Knew this, or Dismiss buttons.
+
+The reviewer uses dedicated reviewer instructions in an ephemeral, read-only
+`codex exec` session in a temporary directory, with AGENTS.md loading, user config,
+hooks, plugins, shell, Code Mode, JavaScript, multi-agent
+tools, goals, and web search disabled. It uses the normal Codex auth store, not
+necessarily a parent session's explicitly selected account or custom provider.
+An additional model request adds usage and up to 35 seconds to turn completion.
+It reviews only the final response, not the code or tool transcript; it is not a
+correctness or security audit. Responses over 12,000 characters are skipped rather
+than truncated. Errors and timeouts fail open, with a diagnostic on hook stderr.
+
+## Use
+
+From this checkout, register the included marketplace and install the plugin:
+
+```sh
+codex-fork plugin marketplace add .
+codex-fork plugin add heads-up@codex-local
+```
+
+Enable `features.hooks` and start a new thread. No Rust rebuild is needed.
+The hook uses `${PLUGIN_ROOT}` supplied by Codex.
+
+The reviewer prefers `codex-fork` on PATH, then `codex`. Set `HEADS_UP_CODEX` to an
+executable path to override it, and `HEADS_UP_MODEL` to override the parent model.
+The executable must support `exec --ignore-user-config --ignore-rules --ephemeral`.
+Disable the plugin to turn off automatic review.
+
+## Verify
+
+```sh
+python3 -m unittest discover -s plugins/heads-up/scripts -p 'test_*.py'
+python3 plugins/heads-up/scripts/heads_up.py --help
+```
+
+A standalone smoke test accepts the same JSON on stdin as a Stop hook:
+
+```sh
+python3 plugins/heads-up/scripts/heads_up.py <<'INPUT'
+{"hook_event_name":"Stop","last_assistant_message":"Added automatic retries to payment calls. All tests pass."}
+INPUT
+```
